 1. for i in 1..3; x = i; end; then          -> i = 3, x = 3
 2. [10, 20].each { |j| y = j }; then        -> after [j * j for j in [10, 20]]: j -> NameError
 3. for v in Bag.new                         -> Bag.__iter__ called; v after the loop = 'b'
 4. while n < 2; w = n; ...; then            -> n = 2, w = 1
 5. times / upto / step / loop               -> inside def count(): t and tt; outside: t -> NameError, tt -> NameError
 6. z = nil; [1].each { |q| z = q }          -> for: z = 1; after `def assign(): z = 2`: z = 1
 7. for a, b in [[1, 2], [3, 4]]; then       -> a = 3, b = 4
 8. for ... end as a value                   -> SyntaxError for x = for ...; after del i: i -> NameError
 9. [1].each { |q; outer| outer = ... }      -> outer = 'outer'
10. for none in []; end; then none           -> none -> NameError
11. lambdas capturing the loop variable      -> for -> [3, 3, 3]; comprehension -> [3, 3, 3]; lambda d=d -> [1, 2, 3]
